---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="Automate real screen reader testing"
   summary="a11ied is a CLI-first toolkit that lets you test with VoiceOver, NVDA, and a fast virtual screen reader — from the terminal, an AI agent, or Storybook. Look up WCAG criteria, check applicability, run interaction patterns, and verify conformance in one workflow."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section class="split panel">
      <div class="stack">
         <div class="panel-head">
            <p class="panel-kicker">Common workflows</p>
            <h2>Pick a starting point</h2>
         </div>
         <div class="workflow-list">
            <div class="workflow-row">
               <strong><a href="/workflows#check-one-criterion">Check one criterion</a></strong>
               <span>Look up a WCAG rule, check if it applies, gather evidence, and verify the result.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="workflow-row">
               <strong><a href="/workflows#verify-a-level">Verify a target level</a></strong>
               <span>Run the full A, AA, or AAA criterion matrix against a page or component.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="workflow-row">
               <strong><a href="/workflows#drive-a-session">Drive a reader session</a></strong>
               <span>Control VoiceOver, NVDA, or the virtual reader directly with low-level commands.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="workflow-row">
               <strong><a href="/workflows#agent-and-storybook">Use it from an agent or Storybook</a></strong>
               <span>Call the same runtime through MCP tool calls or against local Storybook stories.</span>
            </div>
         </div>
      </div>
      <div class="split-aside">
         <div class="tag">tip</div>
         <p class="aside-note">
            Already know the commands? Jump to <a href="/cli-reference">CLI
            reference</a> or <a href="/mcp-usage">MCP usage</a>.
         </p>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="ledger">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">How it works</p>
         <h2>Four steps to a verified result</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="mini-grid">
         <div class="stack">
            <div class="tag">1. Look up the rule</div>
            <p>Use <code>wcag show</code> to pull criterion details, coverage status, and verification strategy.</p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <div class="tag">2. Check applicability</div>
            <p>Use <code>inspect</code> to confirm whether the criterion applies to your page or story.</p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <div class="tag">3. Gather evidence</div>
            <p>Use <code>drive</code> for manual control, <code>run axe</code> for static analysis, or <code>run pattern</code> for reusable interaction probes.</p>
         </div>
         <div class="stack">
            <div class="tag">4. Verify</div>
            <p>Use <code>verify</code> to produce a criterion or level verdict based on the evidence collected.</p>
         </div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Quick start</p>
         <h2>Try it in five minutes</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="command-strip">
         <pre><code>node packages/cli/dist/cli.js doctor
node packages/cli/dist/cli.js wcag show 4.1.3 --json
node packages/cli/dist/cli.js inspect criterion 4.1.3 --url http://127.0.0.1:6173/status-message.html --json
node packages/cli/dist/cli.js run pattern status_message_probe --target virtual --url http://127.0.0.1:6173/status-message.html --json
node packages/cli/dist/cli.js verify criterion 4.1.3 --target virtual --url http://127.0.0.1:6173/status-message.html --json</code></pre>
         <p class="command-note">
         Each step builds on the previous one: look up the rule, check if it applies, run the test,
         then verify.
         </p>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="ledger">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Documentation</p>
         <h2>Explore the docs</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong><a href="/workflows">Workflows</a></strong>
            <span>Step-by-step guides for the most common tasks.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong><a href="/cli-reference">CLI reference</a></strong>
            <span>Full command tree with every subcommand and flag.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong><a href="/wcag-data-sources">WCAG data sources</a></strong>
            <span>Where the standards data comes from and how it stays in sync.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong><a href="/criterion-lookup">Criterion lookup</a> and <a href="/applicability">Applicability</a></strong>
            <span>Find the right criterion and check whether it applies to your target.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong><a href="/driver-usage">Driver usage</a> and <a href="/pattern-execution">Pattern execution</a></strong>
            <span>Low-level screen reader control and reusable interaction probes.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong><a href="/verification-semantics">Verification semantics</a></strong>
            <span>How verdicts work: pass, fail, mixed, manual-only, and not-covered.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong><a href="/mcp-usage">MCP usage</a> and <a href="/storybook-usage">Storybook usage</a></strong>
            <span>Use a11ied from an AI agent (MCP) or against Storybook components.</span>
         </div>
         <div class="route-row">
            <strong><a href="/api-reference">API reference</a> and <a href="/recording-sessions">Recording sessions</a></strong>
            <span>Public package API and video recording of real assistive technology sessions.</span>
         </div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Transparency</p>
         <h2>Transparent verification results</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
         Every verification result reports exactly which checks were automated, which need human review,
         and which criteria aren't covered yet. Each result shows what was proved and what still
         requires manual inspection.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
